{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"length","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","reasoning_content":"We have a problem: count binary words of length 13 that do not contain any forbidden substring \"111\" or \"000\". So we need number of binary strings of length 13 avoiding runs of 3 zeros or 3 ones. This is a combinatorial counting problem. We can solve via recurrence or automaton. Let's compute number of binary strings of length n with no 3 consecutive equal bits. This is like Fibonacci-like. Let a_n be number of strings length n with no 3 consecutive equal bits. We can derive recurrence: For n>=3, a_n = a_{n-1} + a_{n-2}. Wait need to consider states: last two bits. Let's define DP with states: ending with 0,1 and last run length 1 or 2. Let's define:\n\nLet A_n = number of strings length n ending with a single 0 (i.e., last bit 0, previous bit not 0 or n=1). B_n = ending with double 0 (last two bits 00). Similarly C_n = ending with single 1, D_n = ending with double 1.\n\nRecurrence: For n>=2:\nA_{n} = C_{n-1} + D_{n-1} (since to end with single 0, previous bit must be 1, and previous run length can be 1 or 2). Similarly B_n = A_{n-1} (since to have double 0, previous must be single 0). Similarly C_n = A_{n-1} + B_{n-1}. D_n = C_{n-1}.\n\nBase n=1: strings: \"0\" and \"1\". So A_1=1 (single 0), B_1=0, C_1=1, D_1=0.\n\nCompute up to n=13.\n\nLet's compute iteratively.\n\nn=1:\nA1=1, B1=0, C1=1, D1=0.\n\nn=2:\nA2 = C1 + D1 = 1+0=1\nB2 = A1 =1\nC2 = A1 + B1 =1+0=1\nD2 = C1 =1\n\nCheck total a2 = A2+B2+C2+D2 =1+1+1+1=4. All 4 strings length 2 allowed (00,01,10,11). Good.\n\nn=3:\nA3 = C2 + D2 =1+1=2\nB3 = A2 =1\nC3 = A2 + B2 =1+1=2\nD3 = C2 =1\nTotal a3 =2+1+2+1=6. Let's verify: All 8 strings length 3 minus forbidden 000 and 111 => 6. Good.\n\nn=4:\nA4 = C3 + D3 =2+1=3\nB4 = A3 =2\nC4 = A3 + B3 =2+1=3\nD4 = C3 =2\nTotal a4 =3+2+3+2=10. Let's check known sequence: number of binary strings length n with no 3 consecutive equal bits: 2,4,6,10,16,26,... Let's compute further.\n\nn=5:\nA5 = C4 + D4 =3+2=5\nB5 = A4 =3\nC5 = A4 + B4 =3+2=5\nD5 = C4 =3\nTotal a5 =5+3+5+3=16. Good"}}],"created":1790955410,"model":"C:\\Users\\d2j3\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-09-10\\napraw\\outputs\\moon-native\\models\\gpt-oss-20b-MXFP4.gguf","system_fingerprint":"b10809-5266f24da","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":768,"prompt_tokens":3713,"total_tokens":4481,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-9ztUvbY4bnL4Gfje6J31qpBbSdxlm2g6","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":3713,"prompt_ms":447.842,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.12061459736062483,"prompt_per_second":8290.87044091443,"predicted_n":768,"predicted_ms":2332.987,"predicted_per_token_ms":3.041704041720991,"predicted_per_second":328.7630835491153}}